  "cards": [
    {
      "dot": "cyan",
      "title": "Classify enough, not everything",
      "items": [
        "Existing Unity Catalog tags, column masks, and row filters are classification decisions someone already made — harvest them first",
        "An existing mask or row filter is also a migration task, since neither survives a clone",
        "An LLM can draft the candidate list; only the data protection owner signs the final one"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "amber",
      "title": "Provider-constrained isn't a blocked migration",
      "items": [
        "Unity Catalog federation and Delta Sharing govern data where it sits, permanently",
        "This is exactly the case remote governance vs. migration was designed to answer",
        "A residency finding rarely has to stop the whole programme"
      ]
    },
    {
      "dot": "rose",
      "title": "What survives the move besides the bytes",
      "items": [
        "A Unity Catalog metastore is regional — a second jurisdiction means a second metastore",
        "A customer-managed key does not travel; the target needs its own, in the right region",
        "The audit trail proving compliance is destroyed by decommissioning unless exported first"
      ]
    }
  ]
